### 3. Literature Scan (2024–2026)

| 2024–2026 Work / Claim | Idea | Transfers to sub-$L[1/3]$ factoring? | Blocking Repo Barrier |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Tensor-Network / p-bit / VQE Schnorr CVP** (Tesoro et al., `arXiv:2410.16355`, *Phys. Rev. A*; Al-Hasso & von der Leyen, `arXiv:2510.19390`, Oct 2025; `arXiv:2411.16632`) | Cast Schnorr's prime-lattice CVP as spin-glass / tensor-network / p-bit optimization; claim empirical poly scaling up to 100–130 bits. | **No.** At Schnorr's dimension, relations do not exist asymptotically; valid dimensions require $\gamma \to 1$ where spin-glass gaps close exponentially. | [schnorrcvp_results.md:39-44](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/schnorrcvp_results.md#L39-L44), [68-75](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/schnorrcvp_results.md#L68-L75) ($E_{\text{tot}} \approx 10^{-52}$ at 400 bits; $\|uw\| \ge N-1$; $n_{\min} \gtrsim (\ln N)^{3/2}$); [resbarrier_results.md:388](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/resbarrier_results.md#L388). |
| **Smooth Twins via SVP** (Mulder–Sterner–van Woerden, `arXiv:2509.17699` / ePrint `2025/1462`, ANTS XVII 2026) | Find 213-bit $B$-smooth twins $(u, u+1)$ via SVP in Micciancio/Schnorr prime lattices (dense regime). | **No.** Twins sit at $\approx 1.1\lambda_1^{\text{GH}}$ with no target $N$; factoring needs *unplanted* CVP$_{1+O(1/x)}$ in dim $L[1/3]$ or sparsecoset vectors far below GH. | [siconstruct_results.md:106-108](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/siconstruct_results.md#L106-L108), [156-171](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/siconstruct_results.md#L156-L171) (Prop CV); [navigate_results.md:419-424](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/navigate_results.md#L419-L424) (Prop LT(c)). |
| **Subexponential Circuits for $mk!$** (Zhang–Xuan, `arXiv:2610.28338`, Oct 2026) | Unconditional division-free circuit $\tau(mk!) \le \exp(O((\log k)^{2/3}(\log\log k)^{1/3}))$ via genus-2 Jacobians. | **No.** At $k = \lfloor\sqrt{N}\rfloor$, circuit size is $L_N[2/3] \gg L_N[1/3]$, and the uncontrolled multiple $m > 0$ can satisfy $N \mid m$ ($\gcd = N$). | [suffmap_results.md:486-514](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L486-L514) (E4); [slpcirc_results.md:13-19](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/slpcirc_results.md#L13-L19) (Prop R). |
| **Capacity-Achieving Plain RS List Decoders** (Brakensiek et al., `arXiv:2609.08005`; Jeronimo, `arXiv:2609.05870`, Sept 2026) | Decode plain prime-field RS codes to capacity $1-R-\varepsilon$ without folded structure. | **No.** Runtime $q^{O(\varepsilon^{-12/\theta})}$ blows up super-exponentially as agreement $\varepsilon \sim 1/\pi(B) \to 0$; CRT towers $q^e$ lack global Hasse derivations. | [crtdecode_results.md:263-273](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/crtdecode_results.md#L263-L273); [pilist_results.md:352-359](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/pilist_results.md#L352-L359). |
| **Double Index Calculus in $\mathbb{F}_p^*$** (Huang et al., `arXiv:2409.08784`, 2024–2026) | Intersect $g$-relations and target-$b$ relations on shared factor-base primes before full LA. | **No.** Does not alter norm sizes or Dickman $\rho(u)$; saves at most O(1)/LA factors at $\alpha = 1/2$ or $1/3$. | [suffmap_results.md:157-186](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/suffmap_results.md#L157-L186) (Theorem SS: $\omega \le 2$ / LA tricks cannot move single-family exponent). |
| **ExTNFS 4D Sieving & `TNFS-alpha` / Refined NFS $o(1)$** (Robinson–McGuire 2024–2025; Guillevic 2025–2026; Le Gluher–Spaenlehauer–Thomé 2024–2025) | Multi-dimensional orthotope sieving and tower polyselect for $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$; slow $o(1) \sim \frac{4\ln\ln\ln N}{3\ln\ln N}$ expansion. | **No.** $\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$ lacks a known subfield characteristic $p \ll N$; $t \ge 3$ sieving and towers preserve $\alpha = 1/3$ with worse/equal constants. | [heurnfs_results.md:342-380](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/heurnfs_results.md#L342-L380) (Barriers B2 & B3); [rank3_results.md:231-238](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/rank3_results.md#L231-L238). |
| **Provable Quasi-Polynomial Fixed-Char DLP & Smooth Generators** (Lido / KW follow-ups 2024–2025; Bach–Sorenson, ANTS XVII 2026) | Frobenius/elliptic systematic elimination in $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$; fast global generation of factored smooth integers. | **No.** Over $\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$, Witt lifts create $N^{\Theta(1)}$ carries and additive Frobenius already factors $N$; global smooth samplers pay $N/h$ rejection on windows. | [heurnfs_results.md:450-460](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/heurnfs_results.md#L450-L460); [smoothbuild_results.md:520-526](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/smoothbuild_results.md#L520-L526); [siconstruct_results.md:412-415](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/siconstruct_results.md#L412-L415). |
| **Streaming Regev Quantum Factoring / SQUFOF / Base-Sum** (`arXiv:2610.06733` Oct 2026; Murru et al. `arXiv:2409.03486`; Friedlander `arXiv:2504.21168`) | Low-qubit multidimensional lattice period sampling; quadratic forms ($L[1/2]$); binary/decimal sum conversion ($O(\sqrt{N})$). | **No.** Classical simulation of Regev's phase state hits exponential bit-cut Schmidt rank; the classical papers sit at $L[1/2]$ and $N^{1/2}$. | [analytic_results.md:74-80](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/analytic_results.md#L74-L80) (Schmidt rank $\asymp \text{ord}(a)$); [resbarrier_results.md:389](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/resbarrier_results.md#L389). |

---

### 4. Final Ranking of Surviving Mechanisms ($\le 3$)

1. **S1 — Type-D Relative-Rank-$m \ge 3$ Non-Power Linked Modules over Fixed Small $k$ (and Subfield-Free Matroid Degeneracies)** — **$P(\alpha < 1/3, \text{heuristic}) = 0.3\%$**
   - *Why #1:* The only mechanism in the linked-order model whose size–entropy ledger ($\ln X \asymp \sqrt{x\ln x} \implies \alpha = 1/4$) survives Theorem R1, Theorem FH, Prop RR, and our Door-(ii) closure without requiring a new decoding paradigm.
   - *Cheap falsification test:* Over $k = \mathbb{Q}(i)$, $m = 3$ ($r = 6, D = 12$) with general LLL-selected relative cubics $f, g \in \mathbb{Z}[i][x]$ across 30–80-bit split $N$, test whether $\min_{\text{genuine } a \in \{0,\pm 1\}^6} \ln|F(a)|/\ln N$ ever drops below the relative-R1 floor $\frac{e(m-1)}{2n-1} = 0.80$ toward $\frac{e}{d} = 0.33$. (Our Kummer-cubic E3 run already hit `1.81–1.92`.)

2. **S2 — Class-Group Positive-Definite Binary-Quadratic 2D-CRT Beyond-Johnson Constructor (`CG-2D-CRT`)** — **$P(\alpha < 1/3, \text{heuristic}) = 0.15\%$**
   - *Why #2:* Cleanest adaptive constructor in the uncovered sub-Johnson / super-capacity regime ($\text{agreement}/\text{entropy} \asymp (x/\ln x)^\beta \to \infty$) with zero untested residue side and genuine compositeness protection against `navigate` Theorem DLB.
   - *Cheap falsification test:* On 48–80-bit balanced $N$ ($\beta = 1/4$ path), compare Gröbner/multiplicity-interpolation and BP/spectral CRT decoding on $Q_m(k,v) \bmod q^{e_q}$ against 2-D lattice sieving of $[1,K]^2$; kill if operation count per found witness tracks $\Theta(K^2\rho(u_0)^{-1} \text{ or } K^2)$.

3. **S3 — Non-Exact Evaluated Multi-Presentation Split Pencils (`Mod-N Split Pencils`)** — **$P(\alpha < 1/3, \text{heuristic}) = 0.05\%$**
   - *Why #3:* Survives `ptebarrier` Theorem W, `pilist` Lemma PEN, Lemma FT, and Newton's power-sum pigeonhole only via uncontrolled mod-$N$ quotients $N\cdot T_A(X) \ne 0$, with no known constructive handle.
   - *Cheap falsification test:* Census all degree-$M \in \{5,6,7\}$ split polynomials $P_A(X)$ ($B \le 16$) on 24–36-bit $N$ satisfying $|P_A(m) \bmod^* N| \le V$; kill if pairwise-compatible pencil incidence matches the random Poisson baseline $(2V/N)^2$ within $2\sigma$.
